 :interpretation
 {:summary "First DIRECT same-workload same-JVM comparison against a named peer (ADR-2607250100 axis 1). After one-time hydration (~50ms at 3k datoms), kotobase-peer's hot db answers value-point lookups in p50 ~0.004ms -- two orders of magnitude FASTER than Datomic Pro's in-memory query path (p50 ~0.5ms) -- and full scans are comparable (p50 ~3.6ms vs ~3.1ms). Writes are ~8.7x slower (438ms vs 51ms for 3,000 entities): kotobase encrypts every value (AES-256-GCM) + blinds every key (HMAC) + content-addresses every block, which is the zero-trust product cost, not harness overhead."
  :honest-asymmetries ["Datomic's in-memory dev protocol omits its durable transactor+storage write path; kotobase's write path here is its real engine (blocks into an atom)"
                       "kotobase pays a one-time hydrate (~50ms at 3k) per chain-cid before queries; Datomic dbs are always hot"
                       "single-attribute string workload; no joins, no history queries, no concurrent load -- this is a first receipt, not a TPC substitute"]
  :axis-1-status "same-workload direct-comparison gap: first entry closed for Datomic; Neo4j (embedded) and RisingWave (server) head-to-heads remain open."}}
